# Frontend Styling Standards

## Tailwind CSS v4

- Utilities + `@import "./tailwind.css"` (see `src/styles/index.css`).
- Theme colors map to CSS variables (`--background`, `--foreground`, `--card`, `--border`, `--primary`, `--destructive`, etc.) via `@theme inline`.
- Prefer **semantic utilities** (`bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`) over raw `slate-*` on new UI. Legacy pages may still mix slate on layout chrome; migrate toward tokens when touching a file.

## Theme Mode

- `App.tsx` adds `dark` to `document.documentElement`. Tokens in `.dark { … }` define the live palette.
- `html.dark { color-scheme: dark; }` (in `index.css`) keeps native controls (select menus) readable—do not strip this.
- UI code should remain **theme-token-driven** so removing forced dark or adding a toggle does not require rewriting components.

## Color & Contrast (required)

- **Never** hardcode `text-black`, `border-black`, or `hover:bg-black/*` on shared primitives—it breaks dark backgrounds (see `Button` in `components/ui/button.tsx`: uses `text-primary-foreground`, `text-foreground`, `border-input`, etc.).
- **`text-muted-foreground`** on near-black panels can fail WCAG at small sizes. For critical secondary copy (table headers, chart axes, captions, pagination), use explicit readable pairs, e.g. `text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400` or `text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300`, or lighten `--muted-foreground` in `index.css` with intent—not random one-offs.
- **Charts (Recharts):** avoid `fill: "var(--muted-foreground)"` on SVG ticks—many browsers resolve this poorly. Wrap the chart in a container with a readable `text-*` color and use `tick={{ fill: "currentColor" }}` plus `CartesianGrid` with `stroke="currentColor"` and controlled opacity.

## Semantic Roles (reference)

| Role | Tailwind / token |
|------|-------------------|
| Page background | `bg-background` |
| Surfaces / cards | `bg-card`, `text-card-foreground` |
| Borders | `border-border` |
| Primary CTA | `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground` |
| Muted secondary | `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground` (with contrast checks) |
| Destructive | `bg-destructive`, `text-destructive-foreground` |
| Focus ring | `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-background` |

Accent hues (blue for primary nav, emerald/sky/destructive for status) stay **semantic**, not rainbow decoration.

## Layout & rhythm

- **8px grid**: spacing via `gap-4`, `p-4`, `py-6`, etc.
- **Touch targets**: interactive controls ≥ **44px** height where practical (`min-h-[44px]`, `h-11`).
- **Forms**: label stack uses clear separation (`gap-3` between label block and control); labels ≥ `text-sm font-medium text-foreground`; hints use readable muted slate utilities—not cramped `text-xs` glued to controls without spacing.

## Class merging

Use `cn()` from `src/components/ui/utils.ts` (relative imports from pages, e.g. `../components/ui/utils`):

```tsx
import { cn } from "../components/ui/utils";

<div className={cn("rounded-xl border border-border p-4", isActive && "ring-2 ring-ring")} />
```

## UI primitives (`components/ui/`)

- **Button**, **Badge**, **Card**, **Tabs**: CVA variants; extend with tokens, not raw black/white.
- **Native selects**: use **`NativeSelectField`** from `components/ui/native-select.tsx` (chevron, spacing, popover-aligned trigger). Avoid bare `<select>` with ad-hoc classes unless justified.
- No CSS Modules / styled-components—Tailwind utilities only.

## Motion

- UI motion libraries: **`creative-frontend-animation.mdc`** (Motion is default; GSAP/R3F/Rive/Lottie only if requested).
- Prefer **`motion-safe:`** / **`motion-reduce:`** for transitions; avoid `transition-all`—animate specific properties (`colors`, `opacity`, `transform`, `box-shadow`).
